/* @catalog — generated by `npm run catalog:generate`; do not edit by hand.
 * Internal
 *   Types: Change
 *   Functions: db, mutation, code, deferred, createBody, create, current, edit, apply, save, admitLookup,
 *              request, downgrade, capturedAlbumFixture
 *   Constants: actor, other, user, album, artist, first, second, albumTitle, provider
 *   Variables: harness, server, base, token, userToken
 * Tests
 *   - private routing rejects anonymous, ordinary users and mismatched viewer before body; current admin reads shared reviews
 *   - source snapshot retains actual names and missing naming evidence; create receipt replays across source changes
 *   - zero-track Album supports metadata-only review; malformed, excessive, mixed Video and unavailable membership fail closed
 *   - review projects never enter legacy import inventory/read/mutations/asset/duplicate/publication protocols
 *   - source status distinguishes changed metadata and unavailable lifecycle and prevents apply without blocking private draft repair
 *   - legacy file replacement without metadata revision change invalidates filename evidence and apply
 *   - manual edit and provider checkpoint preserve baseline conflict; individual adoption changes only private saved values
 *   - explicit selected apply preserves unrelated metadata, Credits, assets, visibility and membership; receipt and order commit together
 *   - applying selected Track Numbers re-derives the Album order within Disc Numbers
 *   - concurrent private edits have one winner; concurrent application from separate projects cannot overwrite the first
 *   - late apply transaction failure rolls back prior Track updates, Disc Numbers, Album ordering and the review receipt
 *   - review/import share account admission and daily provider budgets; stopped in-flight work still occupies its slot
 *   - ambiguous provider outcome persists and blocks paid replay but allows explicit manual apply
 *   - permission loss and expired analysis grants prevent new provider calls and catalog writes
 *   - separate review inventory supports scoped pagination/counts and terminal applied filtering
 *   - reviews keep the last-administrator-receipt window for edits, adoption and stopping analysis, and never gain automatic values
 *   - a review saved in a newer draft format reads through the Draft v2 allowlist and admits only stopping its analysis
 *   - reviews store Draft v2 with read-only context through edit, analysis and adoption, and review edits bind to the last administrator change
 *   - review context comes from ordered Credits with phrases and the first ready label; it is read-only and Artist suggestions stay hints
 *   - a Luna Disc Number is kept only for a track whose source captured one, and adopting and applying it re-derives the Album order
 *   - a review never reads, sends or records lookup context, even with an applied MusicBrainz release stored under its id
 *   - applying a captured Disc Number writes it as a catalog edit, re-derives the order and commits with the receipt; null clears both keys
 *   - an external Disc Number change makes the source changed and prevents apply
 *   - an oversized review draft is refused at creation and nothing is inserted; the read-only Credits context never counts toward the cap
 *   - Draft v2 reviews are claimed by the worker and count toward actor and deployment analysis capacity
 *   - a review stored before Draft v2 reviews opens converted, stays unconverted on reads, refusals and cancellation, and converts at its first change
 *   - creation from a stale Album revision is a source change that inserts nothing, so the operation can be retried at the current revision
 *   - an edit that grows a review draft past 48 KB is refused and writes nothing; an oversized stored draft still accepts edits that do not grow it
 *   - a pre-Draft v2 review refuses label and visibility edits unconverted, converts once under concurrent edits, and converts when analysis or apply is its first change
 *   - a pre-Draft v2 review whose analysis was queued before deploy converts at a later edit and the worker then suggests against the legacy entry
 *   - an external expected tracklist change makes the source changed and prevents apply
 *   - admitting a review to metadata lookup captures its source, member Credits, attribution and durations, and stores format 3 with one new revision and no receipt
 *   - a review whose source is not current is never admitted to metadata lookup, and nothing is stored
 *   - admission to metadata lookup is idempotent, also for two concurrent admissions, and refuses applied, newer and unreadable reviews
 *   - a review created before Disc Numbers were captured converts through Draft v2 to format 3, gains each Track's disc and can apply a disc-2 change
 *   - per-path review saves write only the sent values as the administrator's own, on formats 2 and 3, and replay
 *   - a whole-draft save is refused on a format-3 review with a reload request, even at a stale revision, and still admitted on format 2
 *   - a review save refuses Artist entries, the label, visibility, the expected tracklist and member entries, on formats 2 and 3, writing nothing
 *   - per-path staleness: an administrator value saved since conflicts and writes nothing, an automatic value only yields on a path the save sends
 *   - the review size cap binds only editable values that grow: a large tracklist and member entries never block a title edit
 *   - review save bodies may reach 160 KB; other review bodies stay at 96 KB
 *   - a format-3 review is analyzed with Draft v2 suggestions, records an adopted value as the administrator's own, applies, and alone shows the review-only values
 *   - admission reads an unmigrated Album's linked Artists as its primaries; unreadable, over-long or unready Credits only make a list incomplete or the label read-only
 *   - a per-path save converts a review stored before Draft v2 with only the sent values as the administrator's own; a refused save converts nothing
 *   - a per-path save replays after the review became format 3, and is refused on a newer format, a format-3 draft missing its review-only values and an applied review
 *   - on a format-3 review an accepted suggestion replaces an automatic value written after its baseline, while an administrator value written since conflicts
 * @end-catalog */

import assert from 'node:assert/strict';
import { randomUUID } from 'node:crypto';
import { after, before, beforeEach, test } from 'node:test';
import type { Server } from 'node:http';
import { ObjectId } from 'mongodb';
